        "text": "Let's start this module with a trading strategy called scalping. While day trading takes place over a day, it's possible to trade on even shorter time frames. Scalpers try to game small fluctuations in price, trading large amounts over minutes or even seconds. Scalpers predominantly use technical analysis to make their trading decisions. The difference between the price people are selling and people are bidding, known as the spread, is also an excellent opportunity for profit. Some investors are willing to buy an asset at a slightly higher price or sell at a slightly lower price in order for their trades to take place instantly.",
